    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Wait, you're saying it's \"direct theft\" and \"fundamentally fails the social contract\"? That sounds pretty one-sided for a news summary. What about the people who say competition actually forces public schools to improve so they don't lose students? Isn't that a valid way to look at it too?",
