    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The \"competition\" argument is a classic libertarian myth that ignores how public schools are already held accountable by standardized testing and funding formulas. In reality, vouchers simply allow the most privileged families to opt out of a failing system, leaving behind a concentrated pool of struggling students who then receive even less funding per pupil. This creates a vicious cycle where public schools become increasingly under-resourced and unable to improve, rather than becoming more efficient. You should present this as the reality of how the system actually functions, not just as a theoretical possibility.",
